{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"web-development","displayName":"Web 开发 · CloudBase Web Development","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/binggg/skills/web-development","publisherHandle":"binggg","publisherDisplayName":"Booker Zhao","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/binggg","version":"1.27.84","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1792378712033,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/web-development/card?ownerHandle=binggg&version=1.27.84","sha256":"6075dd97921bcd6efb2f7459fa682dedbaf7b1e1248c0038fb914763e46f308a","size":2070,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"317ec39e71e5a8c1dbd7e97dca379fde5ff22db292a651d2ef527ec0680e7f29","bundleFingerprints":["963c3a5fc6e058f79a18d94a44104271c44db57160f60986d75e834d1a28bfe8"],"files":[{"path":"LICENSE.md","size":1074,"sha256":"d9dc995e7c280063ca3927b7c47c3d370e1ab6e5db706603175d73199a6b4a71","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":13846,"sha256":"904673de3a51103297dd8e64acd77b0a4a22e854289c36832b1db3006fb35e1a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"browser-testing.md","size":5232,"sha256":"9330e4f6c0ee4f5e8eeb06cc2bb86ed144435562823e3a35f78ebcc1a5e8dfaf","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"frameworks.md","size":6201,"sha256":"2e8239bd16e5e0ed5ec22f9ec394cc7919a1cccc3a2d8db7c02454f64a35a4a5","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This web-development skill is mostly coherent, but its CloudBase auth examples can teach agents to accept unverified tokens as authenticated users.","model":null,"checkedAt":1792379594343,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.2","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"Authentication Bypass in Server-Side Authorization Examples"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"frameworks.md"},"region":{"startLine":60,"endLine":149}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"4e27ebeea4683083"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n\n**File Location**: `frameworks.md`, lines 60–70 and 126–149  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Acceptance of unverified authentication tokens  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```ts\n// app/api/protected/route.ts — Server-side Route Handler\nimport { NextRequest, NextResponse } from \"next/server\"\n\nexport async function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n  const token = request.cookies.get(\"cloudbase_token\")?.value\n  if (!token) {\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"Unauthorized\" }, { status: 401 })\n  }\n  // Verify token with Node SDK or forward to your backend\n  return NextResponse.json({ data: \"protected resource\" })\n}\n```\n\n```ts\n@Injectable()\nexport class CloudBaseAuthGuard implements CanActivate {\n  constructor(@Inject(CLOUDBASE) private cloudbase: any) {}\n\n  async canActivate(context: ExecutionContext): Promise<boolean> {\n    const request = context.switchToHttp().getRequest()\n    const token = request.headers.authorization?.replace(\"Bearer \", \"\")\n    if (!token) return false\n\n    try {\n      // Verify the session via Node SDK\n      // Note: Node SDK does not have a direct \"verify token\" method —\n      // forward the token to a cloud function or use the HTTP API for validation\n      request.user = { token }\n      return true\n    } catch {\n      return false\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nBoth documentation examples treat the presence of attacker-controlled token text as sufficient proof of authentication.\n\nThe Next.js example reads `cloudbase_token` from a request cookie and returns protected data whenever the value is non-empty. Although its comment says to verify the token, the execution path performs no verification.\n\nThe NestJS guard similarly extracts arbitrary text from the `Authorization` header, assigns it to `request.user`, and returns `true`. Its `try/catch` does not provide a security gate because no operation inside the `try` block can validate or reject the token.\n\nNeither example validates the token's cryptographic signature, issuer, audience, expiration, intended CloudBase environment, revocation state, or associated identity. Applications implementing these examples as presented would therefore confuse attacker-supplied input with an authenticated principal.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An application adopts either documented example to protect a server-side endpoint.\n2. The endpoint becomes accessible to a remote network client.\n3. The attacker supplies any non-empty value:\n   - For the Next.js route, the attacker sends a cookie such as `cloudbase_token=invalid`.\n   - For the NestJS guard, the attacker sends a header such as `Authorization: Bearer invalid`.\n4. The application checks only whether token text exists.\n5. No cryptographic or server-side session validation occurs.\n6. The Next.js route returns protected data, or the NestJS guard returns `true` and allows the request to reach the protected handler.\n7. In the NestJS path, downstream code may additionally trust `request.user` even though it contains unverified attacker-controlled data.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA remote unauthenticated attacker can bypass authentication on endpoints protected solely by these examples. The exact scope depends on the adopting application and may include:\n\n- Reading protected application data.\n- Invoking authenticated API operations.\n- Accessing routes intended only for signed-in users.\n- Reaching administrative or user-specific handlers if they rely on this guard.\n- Causing downstream authorization logic to consume attacker-controlled token data as identity information.\n\nThe project is classified as suspicious rather than malicious because the evidence demonstrates insecure guidance and a reachable authorization bypass, but not deliberate backdoor behavior or malicious intent.","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Replace both presence-only checks with a concrete server-side token verification implementation.\n2. Fail closed if a supported verification mechanism is unavailable; do not authorize a request based only on a non-empty cookie or header.\n3. Validate at least:\n   - Cryptographic signature.\n   - Trusted issuer.\n   - Intended audience.\n   - Expiration and not-before claims.\n   - Intended CloudBase environment or tenant.\n   - Revocation or active-session status where supported.\n4. Construct `request.user` exclusively from verified claims returned by the trusted verification service. Never store the raw unverified token as the authenticated identity.\n5. Ensure malformed `Authorization` headers are rejected. Require the exact expected authentication scheme and token format.\n6. Update the documentation so its examples are secure and executable rather than leaving the essential verification step as a comment.\n7. Add negative tests confirming rejection of:\n   - Arbitrary non-empty token strings.\n   - Expired tokens.\n   - Tokens with invalid signatures.\n   - Tokens issued for another audience or environment.\n   - Missing or malformed bearer schemes."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":60,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1792379516.8944545,"endTime":1792379566.809494}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"web-development","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57dkqjrafm8qzv6t4rt7cv3xh8gjrms-EtrEgJ/clawscan-skillspector-79469101/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-10-19T03:11:55.988289+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":14,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"MEDIUM"},"components":[{"path":"LICENSE.md","type":"markdown","lines":21,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1074,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":208,"executable":false,"size_bytes":13846,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"browser-testing.md","type":"markdown","lines":71,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5232,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"frameworks.md","type":"markdown","lines":188,"executable":false,"size_bytes":6201,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-2c838ef113724b7b8f0974ee9ab339fd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"frameworks.md","start_line":124,"end_line":149},"finding":null,"explanation":"The NestJS AuthGuard example is presented as token verification, but it only checks for the presence of a Bearer token and then unconditionally sets request.user and returns true. In a web-development skill, developers may copy this pattern directly into production, allowing any attacker with any arbitrary token string to bypass authentication and access protected routes.","remediation":"Replace the placeholder logic with actual server-side token validation before granting access. Use a supported verification flow with @cloudbase/node-sdk, a trusted backend, or a Cloud Function/HTTP API that validates token signature, expiry, issuer, and audience; reject invalid tokens with 401, and clearly label any non-validating snippet as pseudocode or incomplete example code.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"frameworks.md","start_line":124,"end_line":149}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-1914fbb45dca4b83ac3ba01e0f30c412","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"frameworks.md","start_line":31,"end_line":31},"finding":null,"explanation":"The example initializes the SDK with a default region of \"ap-shanghai\" when no user- or deployment-selected value is provided. This imposes a locale/region choice in natural-language guidance and code sample defaults without offering an explicit opt-in or documenting a justified region-specific constraint.","remediation":"Avoid hardcoding a region default unless the skill is explicitly region-specific. Require the region to be configured explicitly, or document that the example applies only to deployments targeting that region and offer alternatives.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"frameworks.md","start_line":31,"end_line":31}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":2714,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":1792,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":2728},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":1605,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":1619},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":5019,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":4864,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":5033},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3378,"c